---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url";

const trajectory = [
  ["2022-23", "Data science and classical machine learning."],
  ["Late 2023-24", "First LLM/RAG systems as a user and builder of applied workflows."],
  ["Late 2025", "First owned RAG and agent systems with evaluation: the shift from using models to engineering them."],
  ["2026", "Production agent-reliability work plus scientific AI: context engineering, evaluation harnesses, multi-agent runtimes, and scientific agents."],
];
---

<Base
  title="Technical Evolution — SciencesLoop"
  description="A public technical evolution record: from scientist to Scientific AI systems builder, grounded in commit history and evidence-backed capability layers."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="page-hero compact">
      <span class="eyebrow">Technical Evolution · evidence-backed narrative</span>
      <h1>From Scientist to Scientific AI Systems Builder</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Not a pivot, but a continuous progression: turning hard domains into
        data, workflows, models, and reliable systems, one abstraction level at
        a time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>The trajectory</h2>
    </div>
    <section class="workflow-steps">
      {trajectory.map(([when, text]) => (
        <article>
          <span>{when}</span>
          <h2>{when}</h2>
          <p>{text}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="workflow-panel">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Capability stack</span>
        <h2>Scientific discovery ← multi-agent systems ← context engineering ← evaluation harness ← foundation models.</h2>
        <p>
          The scarce value is in the middle: context, state, evaluation,
          provenance, and human review. Foundation models matter, but they do
          not make a scientific system reliable by themselves.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="evolution-figures" aria-label="Technical evolution figures">
      <figure>
        <img src={u("/images/evolution/commits_by_theme.png")} alt="Stacked bar chart showing commits by theme over time." loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Commits by theme over time, from the local career-evolution audit.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src={u("/images/evolution/vocab_drift.png")} alt="Vocabulary drift chart showing agent, evaluation, context, and scientific concepts rising in 2026." loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Vocabulary shift toward agent, evaluation, context, and scientific-system concepts in 2026.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="workflow-panel">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Honest note</span>
        <h2>The timeline matters.</h2>
        <p>
          The LLM and agent building spans roughly two years. The
          agent-reliability and scientific-AI depth is concentrated in 2026 and
          anchored in production work. The point is not chasing hype; it is
          continuously engineering AI to be reliable, then turning that
          discipline toward scientific discovery.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        <a class="more" href={u("/approach/")}>Approach →</a>
        {" · "}
        <a class="more" href={u("/programs/#case-studies")}>Case Studies →</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
